    "title": "Tuberculosis exposure identified at Pleasant Knoll Middle School in Fort Mill - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Bailey Striepling ,\n1 hours ago FORT MILL, S.C. ( QUEEN CITY NEWS ) — The South Carolina Department of Public Health has identified an exposure to tuberculosis at Pleasant Knoll Middle School in Fort Mill.\nOfficials have not said how many people may have been exposed to the TB germ.\nState health officials are working with Fort Mill Schools to identify individuals who may need testing.\nTB can be treated with antibiotics. Additional information, including frequently asked questions, can be found on DPH’s website or the CDC’s website .\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Queen City News.",
    "summary": "1 hours ago FORT MILL, S.C. ( QUEEN CITY NEWS ) — The South Carolina Department of Public Health has identified an exposure to tuberculosis at Pleasant Knoll Middle School in Fort Mill. Officials have not said how many people may have been exposed to the TB germ. State health officials are working with Fort Mill Schools to identify individuals who may need testing. Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.",
